# Product Context

This project is a realistic business CRM / Client Management System demo.

The goal is NOT to build a SaaS startup right now.

The goal is:

- showcase production-quality business system skills
- attract real clients
- reuse architecture later
- evolve into SaaS only if strong patterns emerge

This app must feel like a real product, not a CRUD tutorial.

# Product Philosophy

The application should communicate:

"I can build real business systems."

NOT:

"I can generate admin panels."

Product thinking is more important than CRUD implementation.

# UX Direction

Prioritize:

- workflow clarity
- polished interactions
- realistic business flows
- responsiveness
- spacing consistency
- visual hierarchy
- typography quality
- perceived quality

Always include:

- loading states
- skeletons
- polished empty states
- hover states
- transitions
- optimistic updates where reasonable
- realistic seeded data

Avoid:

- lorem ipsum
- fake tutorial-style dashboards
- generic admin templates
- overcrowded screens
- excessive charts

# Visual Direction

Preferred style:

- premium dark aesthetic
- elegant spacing
- modern SaaS/product feel
- boutique software quality
- clean layouts

Avoid:

- bootstrap admin appearance
- cyberpunk visuals
- neon overload
- cluttered UI

# Architecture Direction

Architecture priorities:

- clarity
- maintainability
- fast iteration
- clean FSD structure
- reusable patterns
- KISS

Do not over-engineer.

# Technical Context

Stack:

- React
- TypeScript
- TanStack Router
- TanStack Query
- HeroUI
- Tailwind CSS
- Supabase
- React Hook Form
- Zod
- Paraglide/Inlang
